# Shopify Theme Conventions

## Section architecture

- Every section: fully customisable from the theme editor. A non-technical merchant controls everything.
- Schema: typed settings, descriptive labels, sensible defaults, block support where appropriate.
- Presets: at least one default preset per section.
- Sections for page-level composition, snippets for reusable sub-components.
- Section groups for header/footer.

## Liquid

- Clean, well-commented code.
- Use `{% comment %}` for section documentation.
- Assign complex logic to variables at top of file before markup.
- Use `| escape` on user-generated content.
- Prefer `render` over `include` for snippets.

## Tailwind CSS (v4)

- Utility-first in templates.
- All custom values come from `@theme inline` in `src/v3.input.css` (extends design system tokens).
- Never hardcode colours, spacing, or font sizes — use Tailwind classes.
- `@apply` only in component CSS files, never in Liquid templates.
- Responsive: mobile-first breakpoint approach.
- This project uses Tailwind v4 (CSS-first). There is no `tailwind.config.js`.

## Capsize typography

- All V3 text styles use Capsize-generated classes (`.text-{style-name}`) from `assets/capsize-v3.css`.
- Never set `font-size` or `line-height` directly in templates. Capsize trims browser leading so text spacing matches Figma.
- When a section introduces a new text style, define it in `src/capsize-v3.js` and regenerate with `npm run capsize:v3`.
- Text style definitions include responsive font-size/line-height per breakpoint.

## React islands

- Liquid vs React is a per-feature decision. Evaluate with George — do not default to React.
- When React is warranted: Liquid section renders the container with data attributes (`<div data-component="ComponentName" data-props='{{ props | json }}'>`).
- React mounts into the container, hydrates from data attributes.
- Storefront API for data beyond Liquid context.

## Accessibility & performance

- Semantic markup, ARIA attributes, keyboard navigation, focus management. WCAG 2.1 AA.
- Mobile-first as a performance concern: asset weight, deferred loading, render cost.
- Canadian English (colour, favourite, centre).
- Sentence case for UI copy.

## Naming

Follow existing theme conventions. Do not impose a new convention without confirming with George.
